n","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/charliermuseum.be","email":"info@charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50005592"},"cn":{"name":"Exposition Albert Dupuis Foundation","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/charliermuseum.be","email":"info@charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50005592"},"fr":{"name":"Exposition Albert Dupuis Foundation","shortdescr":"\n","longdescr":"Voyages vers l'histoire de l'humanit\u00e9\n\nPour c\u00e9l\u00e9brer le centenaire d\u2019Albert Dupuis (1923-2010), le mus\u00e9e Charlier pr\u00e9sente pour la troisi\u00e8me fois son travail. Cet artiste est \u00e0 la fois peintre d\u2019id\u00e9es, arch\u00e9ologue de l\u2019histoire de l\u2019humanit\u00e9, homo universalis, dessinateur ludique, conf\u00e9rencier aux vivaces r\u00e9parties, \u2026 homme aux multi-facettes.\n\n Cette exposition illustre les perp\u00e9tuels changements g\u00e9ographiques et culturels des civilisations, et comment l\u2019art pass\u00e9 et pr\u00e9sent de tous les peuples ont enrichi d\u2019autres cultures.\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/charliermuseum.be","email":"info@charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50005592"},"sp":{"name":"Exposition Albert Dupuis Foundation","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/charliermuseum.be","email":"info@charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50005592"},"nl":{"name":"Tentoonstelling Albert Dupuis Foundation","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":" Om de 100ste verjaardag van Albert Dupuis (1923-2010) te vieren, presenteert het Mus\u00e9e Charlier zijn werk voor de derde keer. Als geen ander was hij een idee\u00ebnschilder, een archeoloog van de menselijke geschiedenis, een homo universalis, een speelse tekenaar, een spreker met een levendige babbel, \u2026 een man met vele facetten.\n\n Deze expo illustreert de geografische en culturele veranderingen van beschavingen en hoe oude en huidige kunst cultureel kan verrijken.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/charliermuseum.be","email":"info@charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50005592"}},"place":{"id":753,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"Das 1928 eingeweihte Museum ist wie ein Gem\u00e4lde der Epoche... man findet sich in der Zeit der La Libre Est\u00e9tique und der Groupe des 20 wieder. Die Sammlungen werden in den reich mit Mobiliar und historischen Dekorationsgegenst\u00e4nden (Louis XV, Louis XV und Empire) best\u00fcckten Salons ausgestellt.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Charlier Museum","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"The museum is based in the private mansion, dating from the 19th century, of the sculptor Guillaume Charlier. It focuses on Belgian painting from the late 19th to the early 20th century. Its art exhibitions take place in a setting of lavish furnishings, with numerous decorative pieces from the Louis XV, Louis XVI, and Empire periods.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"Le mus\u00e9e, inaugur\u00e9 en 1928, est comme un tableau d\u2019\u00e9poque\u2026 on se retrouve au temps de La Libre Esth\u00e9tique et du Groupe des 20. Les collections sont expos\u00e9es dans les salons, riches en mobilier et objets d\u2019art d\u00e9coratifs d\u2019\u00e9poque Louis XV, Louis XVI et Empire.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Museo Charlier","address_street_name":"Avenue des Arts","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Avenue des Arts, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"El Museo Charlier, una mansi\u00f3n del siglo XIX obra de Horta durante sus a\u00f1os de juventud, te sumergir\u00e1 en la atm\u00f3sfera de un lujoso sal\u00f3n de arte: la Belle Epoque te invita a so\u00f1ar, a pasear entre las esculturas de Charlier, Hager y Wouters, las pinturas de Smits, Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric, Oleffe, Laermans, Van Strydonck, Ensor... Este ambiente \u00edntimo se completa con los muebles de los ebanistas Chapuis, Sen\u00e9, Nadal l'A\u00een\u00e9, numerosos objetos de arte decorativo de estilos Luis XIV, XV, XVI y estilo Imperio, tapices de Bruselas y Audenaerde, as\u00ed como excepcionales un excepcional sal\u00f3n chino. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Charliermuseum","address_street_name":"Kunstlaan","address_street_number":"16","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@charliermuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.charliermuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 81 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 217 81 61","address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Kunstlaan, 16","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"Het museum, geopend in 1928, is gevestigd in het prive-herenhuis van de beeldhouwer Guillaume Charlier, dat dateert uit de 19e eeuw. Het richt zich op de Belgische schilderkunst van eind 19e tot begin 20e eeuw. De collecties worden getoond in de salons, rijkelijk voorzien van decoratieve stukken uit de Louis XV, Louis XVI en Empire periodes.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":152,"location":{"lat":50.84755959,"lon":4.36997724},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2023-09-21T14:26:08+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:19+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":276597,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Commune de Saint-Josse-ten-Noode","address_street_name":null,"address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"ad