,"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":[],"recurring":[{"day":"tuesday","occurences":{"is_second":true,"is_third":true,"is_fourth":true,"is_last":true,"is_first":true},"time_start":"10:00:00","time_end":"11:00:00","translations":{"fr":"Ouvert les premier, deuxi\u00e8me, troisi\u00e8me, quatri\u00e8me et dernier mardis du mois de 10:00 \u00e0 11:00","nl":"Open op de eerste, tweede, derde, vierde en laatste dinsdags van de maand van 10:00 tot 11:00","en":"Open the first, second, third, fourth and last tuesdays of the month from 10:00 to 11:00"}}],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[]},{"id":50004781,"date_start":"2024-01-24","date_end":"2024-01-24","date_next":"2024-01-24","accept_article27":true,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":true,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2023-11-28T12:30:01+01:00","published_at":"2023-11-28T12:19:54+01:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":289511,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"concert","ranking":1.2599210498948732,"languages":{"spoken":["nl","en","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":1,"translations":{"de":"Konzert","pt":null,"en":"Concert","it":"Concerti","cn":null,"fr":"Concert","sp":"Concierto","nl":"Concert"}},"others":{"list":[6,4],"translations":{"de":["Worldmusic, Folk & Country","Pop, Rock, Jazz..."],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Worldmusic, Folk & Country","Pop, rock, jazz\u2026"],"it":["Worldmusic, Folk e Country","Pop, rock, jazz\u2026"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Worldmusic, Folk & Country","Pop, rock, jazz\u2026"],"sp":["Worldmusic, folk y country","Pop, rock, jazz\u2026"],"nl":["Worldmusic, Folk & Country","Pop, rock, jazz\u2026"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"pt":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"en":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":"The two new projects of Ver\u00f3nica Codesal, singer in the Ialma group and professor at the Muziekpublique academy, will be highlighted during this evening. Alfaia is a project at the crossroads between Galician musical culture and that of the Maghreb. In the second project, we find Ver\u00f3nica alongside Damien Chierini (violin), Didier Laloy (accordion) and Boris Chango (drums).","longdescr":"The two new projects of Ver\u00f3nica Codesal, singer in the Ialma group and professor at the Muziekpublique academy, will be highlighted during this evening.\n\nAlfaia is a project at the crossroads between Galician musical culture and that of the Maghreb, combining the magnificent voice of Ver\u00f3nica, the warm oud sounds and the viola of Adil Benhsain. Intertwining the traditional rhythms of their two cultures. This beautiful musical adventure, which began during \u201cPremi\u00e8re Esquisse\u201d of the radio program \u201cLe Monde est un Village\u201d, undulates between Galicia and the Maghreb in a surprising and unprecedented way. Noticeable by a repertoire of traditional music and songs , mixed with fine classic touches and reinterpreted in very personal tones. It\u2019s beautiful, it\u2019s delicate, it\u2019s luminous. We can close our eyes and let go\u2026\n\nIn the second project, we find Ver\u00f3nica alongside Damien Chierini (violin), Didier Laloy (accordion) and Boris Chango (drums). With 100 Voltas they want to show the alive side of Galician culture and its constantly evolving tradition. By choosing a repertoire that preserves the heritage of the past, they add contemporary elements and different instruments: electronic instruments, violin, diatonic accordion, etc. Through traditional texts, personal poetic writings or even works by contemporary Galician authors (Lucia Aldao, Yolanda Casta\u00f1o, Rosalia Fern\u00e1ndez Rial, Brais Fernandes), they honor women, wives, mothers, daughters, friends, workers, artists and activists who are the basis of the stories into which they transport the public.","performers":"Ver\u00f3nica Codesal: voice, percussion\nAdil Benhsain: oud, viola, voice, percussion\n\nVeronica Codesal: vocals, percussion\nDamien Chierini: violin, electronics\nDidier Laloy: accordion\nBoris Chango: drumsVer\u00f3nica Codesal: voice, percussion\nAdil Benhsain: oud, viola, voice, percussion","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"it":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"cn":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"fr":{"name":"Musiques de Galice: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":"Les deux nouveaux projets de Ver\u00f3nica Codesal, chanteuse du groupe Ialma et professeure \u00e0 Muziekpublique, seront mis \u00e0 l'honneur \u00e0 l'occasion de cette soir\u00e9e. Alfaia est n\u00e9 de la rencontre entre la culture musicale galicienne et celle du Maghreb. Dans le second projet, on la retrouve aux c\u00f4t\u00e9s de Damien Chierini, Didier Laloy et Boris Chango. ","longdescr":"Les deux nouveaux projets de Ver\u00f3nica Codesal, chanteuse au sein du groupe Ialma et professeure \u00e0 l\u2019acad\u00e9mie de Muziekpublique, seront mis \u00e0 l\u2019honneur \u00e0 l\u2019occasion de cette soir\u00e9e.\n\nAlfaia est un projet n\u00e9 de la rencontre entre la culture musicale galicienne et celle du Maghreb, alliant la voix magnifique de Ver\u00f3nica et les sons chaleureux du oud et de l\u2019alto d\u2019Adil Benhsain, entrem\u00ealant les rythmes traditionnels de leurs deux cultures. Cette belle aventure musicale, qui a d\u00e9but\u00e9 lors de \u00ab Premi\u00e8re Esquisse \u00bb de l\u2019\u00e9mission radio \u00ab Le Monde est un Village \u00bb, ondule entre la Galice et le Maghreb de mani\u00e8re surprenante et in\u00e9dite : en t\u00e9moigne un r\u00e9pertoire de musiques et de chants traditionnels, m\u00e2tin\u00e9s de fines touches classiques et r\u00e9interpr\u00e9t\u00e9s dans des tonalit\u00e9s toutes personnelles. C\u2019est beau, c\u2019est d\u00e9licat, c\u2019est lumineux. On ferme les yeux et on l\u00e2che prise\u2026\n\nDans le second projet, on retrouve Ver\u00f3nica aux c\u00f4t\u00e9s de Damien Chierini (violon), Didier Laloy (accord\u00e9on) et Boris Chango (batterie). Avec 100 Voltas, ils veulent montrer le c\u00f4t\u00e9 vivant de la culture galicienne et sa tradition en constante \u00e9volution. En choisissant un r\u00e9pertoire qui pr\u00e9serve l\u2019h\u00e9ritage du pass\u00e9, ils y ajoutent des \u00e9l\u00e9ments contemporains et diff\u00e9rents instruments : instruments \u00e9lectroniques, violon, accord\u00e9on diatonique,\u2026 \u00c0 travers des textes traditionnels, des \u00e9crits po\u00e9tiques personnels ou encore des \u0153uvres d\u2019auteurs galiciens contemporains (Lucia Aldao, Yolanda Casta\u00f1o, Rosalia Fern\u00e1ndez Rial, Brais Fernandes), ils mettent \u00e0 l\u2019honneur les femmes, les \u00e9pouses, les m\u00e8res, les filles, les ami.es, les travailleur.ses, les artistes et les militant.es qui peuplent les histoires dans lesquelles ils emm\u00e8nent le public.","performers":"Ver\u00f3nica Codesal : voix, percussions\nAdil Benhsain : oud, alto, voix, percussions\n\nVeronica Codesal: voix, percussions\nDamien Chierini: violon, \u00e9lectronique\nDidier Laloy: accord\u00e9on\nBoris Chango : batterie","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"sp":{"name":"The music of Galicia: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"},"nl":{"name":"Galicische muziek: Alfaia & 100 Voltas","shortdescr":"Op deze avond stellen we de twee nieuwe projecten voor met Veronica Codesal, zangeres bij Ialma en leerkracht aan de Muziekpublique academie. Alfaia is de ontmoeting tussen de Galicische muziekcultuur en die van de maghreb. In 100 Voltas vinden we Veronica terug aan de zijde van Damien Chierini, Didier Laloy en drummer Boris Tchango.","longdescr":"Op deze avond stellen we de twee nieuwe projecten voor met Veronica Codesal, zangeres bij Ialma en leerkracht aan de Muziekpublique academie.\n\nAlfaia is de ontmoeting tussen de Galicische muziekcultuur en die van de maghreb, tussen de oorstrelende stem van Ver\u00f3nica en de warme klanken van Adil Benhsain\u2019s oud en altviool, tussen traditionele ritmes uit beide culturen. Na een premi\u00e8re tijdens Premi\u00e8re Esquisse van het radio-programma Le Monde est un Village, startte een prachtig muzikaal avontuur dat op een totaal verrassende en ongekende manier tussen Galici\u00eb en de Maghreb meandert: een repertoire van traditionele muziek en liederen, vermengd met fijne klassieke accenten en geherinterpreteerd in zeer persoonlijke toonaarden.\n\nIn 100 Voltas vinden we Veronica terug aan de zijde van Damien Chierini (viool, effecten), Didier Laloy (accordeon) en drummer Boris Tchango. Voeg daar nog Met 100 Voltas willen ze de Galicische cultuur tonen als een wervelende, levende traditie in voortdurende evolutie. Ze kiezen voor een repertoire dat de essentie van het verleden behoudt maar er hedendaagse elementen en verschillende instrumenten aan toevoegt: elektronische instrumenten, viool, diatonische accordeon,.. Via traditionele teksten, eigen po\u00ebzie en werk van hedendaagse Galicische dichters (Lucia Aldao, Yolanda Casta\u00f1o, Rosalia Fern\u00e1ndez Rial, Brais Fernandes) vertellen ze verhalen over vrouwen, echtgenotes, partners, moeders, dochters, vrienden, arbeiders, kunstenaars en activisten.","performers":"Ver\u00f3nica Codesal (Spanje\/Galicia): stem, percussie\nAdil Benhsain (Marokko): oud, altviool, stem, percussie\n\nVeronica Codesal: stem, percussie\nDamien Chierini: viool, electronica\nDidier Laloy: accordeon","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/muziekpublique.be\/","email":"info@muziekpublique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 217 26 00","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50004781"}},"place":{"id":238099,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Muziekpublique","address_street_name":"